NNAAMMEE
     pprrooccddeesscc — process descriptor facility

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     pprrooccddeesscc is a file-descriptor-oriented interface to process signalling
     and control, which supplements historic UNIX fork(2) and kill(2), primi‐
     tives with new system calls such as pdfork(2) and pdkill(2), pprrooccddeesscc is
     designed for use with capsicum(4), replacing process identifiers with ca‐
     pability-oriented references.  However, it can also be used independently
     of capsicum(4), displacing PIDs, which may otherwise suffer from race
     conditions.  Given a process descriptor, it is possible to query its con‐
     ventional PID using pdgetpid(2).

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     fork(2), kill(2), kqueue(2), pdfork(2), pdgetpid(2), pdkill(2), wait4(2),
     capsicum(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     pprrooccddeesscc first appeared in FreeBSD 9.0, and was developed at the Univer‐
     sity of Cambridge.

